# CODEOWNERS — routes review requests. It does NOT gate merges.
#
# Branch protection on the default branch requires `ci-passed` and nothing else:
# `required_pull_request_reviews` is off, so no review is required from anyone
# named here. GitHub will request a review when a pull request touches an owned
# path, and the pull request can merge without it.
#
# Who may merge, and what actually holds a change, is in GOVERNANCE.md. If this
# file is ever meant to gate, branch protection has to change first — a file
# claiming enforcement it does not have is worse than no file.
#
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-security/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

